MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_001: There. Now we are alone.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_002: Yes, because you sent everyone else away. I take it\nsomething's on your mind?
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_003: I merely thought we might exchange views as\ntwo royals of equal station.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_004: I would know your thoughts on how to divide the\nland of Dagda after the war.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_005: And I wouldn't share them. I see this sort of talk as\nwhat led to disaster in Cydonia.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_006: I, meanwhile, see it as an opportunity to fulfill the\nlong-held dream of the people of Saramis.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_007: Do you know Cybele, the site of the former kingdom\nof Damascar?
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_008: That cursed land containing Ahm Lu, the city of\ndeath? The miasma never clears from there.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_009: Precisely. I want to claim it for Saramis.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_010: It was Dagda the Great who decreed that Cybele\nbe a void region. But he is no more.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_011: The Divine Sovereign Solel promised me that he\nwould investigate the matter, but he too is gone.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_012: So in theory, there is nothing stopping anyone from\nsetting foot in that land.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_013: Well, I've heard the land of Cybele remains\nunsettled.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_014: Legalities aside, I doubt anyone would have an\ninterest in denying your request.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_015: I certainly have no objection as king of Brezarant.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_016: Thank you. But only I have spoken so far. Let us\nhear your feelings on the future shape of the world.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_017: Yes...my feelings.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_018: I wish to take all of it, Saramis excepted. That can\nbe yours.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_019: Pardon me?
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_020: Brezarant will absorb the Dagdan Empire, the\nkingdom of Arago, and all their territories.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_021: That is extraordinarily ambitious. Do you not worry\nyou will sow the seeds of a new war?
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_022: What you call ambitious, I'd call pragmatic.\nYou know of the turmoil rocking Dagda.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_023: With the old order shattered, the borders between\nnations are already less distinct.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_024: Even if the Brimstone Lords are defeated, the people\nwill live in fear of bandits and famine.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_025: But I can quell their fears—unite the three kingdoms\ninto one.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_026: The Dagdan Alliance. That is my vision.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_027: Then you would come not as conqueror of the land\nof Dagda but as its liberator.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_028: I'm not deluded. I know the path ahead is strewn\nwith outcry and uprising.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_029: Nevertheless, I intend to make a world free of\noppression.
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_030: Hmph. This, to you, is not ambitious?
MID_SE_Seo_Bel_B_031: But I will see what becomes of this plan. I've lofty\nexpectations for you, honest and upright king.
